## SEVERITY / VERDICT (decided HERE)
*Blocker:* a product byte or a byte outside the 4 paths in T; an existing test removed or weakened; a word added; a secret; a merged build with a warning or error, or a red merged test run not red at main; the head moved; a security-shaped finding is a STOP, never graded. *Major:* a row with no kill among your GX for its claimed defect (a row that cannot fail), unless the mutant is proved EQUIVALENT; a literal that echoes the product and is wrong by your derivation; a FALSE or unmeasured sentence or count in your squash text; a builder claim contradicted with a verdict consequence (3922 / 3986, 203 -> 243, "9 of 9 red"). *Note:* a green block stated as N runs; A2's whole-number volume against the ticket's words if the Acceptance is met; C3 pinning per-listing counting (if the product owner rules it should read 1, product and C3 change together); the dropped Api half (an open clause); a mutant EQUIVALENT ON A ROW; a FALSE sentence in an uncarried commit message; unsigned commits; Linux, hosted CI, CodeQL NOT RUN; Api wall time against 20 minutes. Say which rule applied to every finding with a fix-shape in prose. Round 1 of 2: do not pad a Note into a NO GO or soften a Major: quote row, input, expected, observed.
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs steps 0-5 measured with controls, c0 and c1 green, c-fail met, every row killed, the local CI line green on the merged tree, every NOT RUN named. GO WITH FINDINGS = Note only (say "NO PR; hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN" on the line above the verdict line). NO GO on any Blocker or Major, class named, "round 1 of 2". **First line of STATUS (placeholder at Step 0 `GATE VERDICT B1106: PENDING`; final, ONE line):** `GATE VERDICT B1106: branch b1094/mps-test-rows-357-362-343-344 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ 14e4d67 on main <sha7> (round 1 of 2 on class "mps: tests-only residue rows of the quantity, projection and panel-parity gates", NO GO 0 before; NO PR, hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN - delta <3 commits, 4 paths, +a -r; paths beyond 4 n; product bytes n; assertions removed n> - overlap <n> - merged CI <build rc, warnings n; test rc; per project files/tests/passed/failed/skipped; N runs> - rows alone <n of 45> - literals <re-derived n of 4|NOT TESTED> - mutants <c0 c1; GX n of n killed; equivalent n; survivors n; c-fail y/n> - ticket clauses <357 n/n, 362 n/n with the Api half open, 343 n/n, 344 n/n> - commit sentences true n of n - squash text true y/n - gitleaks rc <n> - squash files checked y/n)`. Last line exactly one of `VERDICT: B1106 branch b1094/mps-test-rows-357-362-343-344 @ 14e4d67 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> (round 1 of 2) on main <sha7>` (finding ids with severities, the class and "NO PR; hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN" on the line above; no landing word) or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`. **LANDING HOLD (Tuesday's):** after a GO or GO WITH FINDINGS Tuesday opens the PR, reads the hosted checks and alerts at the same head, lands the SAME commit through CodeQL, head-pinned, with your files; nothing deploys. **STATUS-NOW:** STATUS at Step 0 with the placeholder first line and a moving `WORKING: <part> <time>` last line, updated after every check (superseded lines marked); RESUME at about 80 percent of context or the hard stop (`## PROGRESS and RESUME`: done/partial per step, next exact commands, every tree and mutant with restore proof; end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY continue in a fresh seat from RESUME`).
**FOR TUESDAY (what STATUS carries).** Verdict in words with class and round; the property in one paragraph; merged CI table (main and M, per project); per-row table (alone runs, kill list by GX, ticket clause verdict); mutant table in one paragraph with c-fail; the dropped Api half stated as open; the landing tree (T, M, overlaps, web and tools tree equality); squash subject and body (four files) and the exact merge line; the three commit messages each judged, carried or not; stale or false statements in the builder STATUS (its BLUF's "eight ticket items", its READY line's "A1 A2 B1 B2 B3 C1 C2 C3 minus the dropped"); the LANDING CHECKLIST.
**REFUSE AT ONCE** (last line `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY`; each count with a control that can fail): a four-underscore run left in your Step-0 copy (`/usr/bin/grep -c -E '_''_''_''_'`; control: the unstamped `.pre-stamp` copy, if kept, reads 8) or a last line not `READ-WHOLE-BY-TUESDAY: DONE ...` or a `## Stamp` naming no launch authority or hard-stop time; pane not `Datasec/MPS-G279` (`tmux display -p -t "$TMUX_PANE" '#{@cockpit_name}'`; control `-t %0` prints `tuesday`) or a second one lists; the head moved (`ls-remote origin refs/heads/b1094/mps-test-rows-357-362-343-344` is not `14e4d67089045807f292e650ac6d99ff9d93c7db`; a failed call is UNKNOWN: retry 5 times about 10 s apart); a PR now exists for the branch (do not stop: name it, read its checks, add to step 6); main moved past `19d084fa`: STOP only if a moved path is among the branch's 4 paths; any other moved path is named, M rebuilt on the new main and steps 1 and 3 re-derived (a move under `src/` or `tests/` re-runs the anchors; a move outside `src/`, `tests/`, `Directory.Build.props`, `global.json`, `*.csproj`, `MpsCalc.slnx`, `.github/` with a clean overlap does not force the merged run: say which rule you applied); `.tools/b1106` or any `.tools/wt-b1106-*` exists before your own mkdir; the builder STATUS last line not beginning `READY FOR QA: B1094 b1094/mps-test-rows-357-362-343-344 @ 14e4d67089045807f292e650ac6d99ff9d93c7db` (drafter 1; control with a wrong sha 0); no `## PRIOR WORK` in the builder STATUS (drafter: line 19 of 148); `gh auth status` not a Datasec account (say "the project account"; never quote the login); the model not Sonnet (`"model_id": "claude-sonnet-5-5"` at `models_latest.json:23`; the launch carries `BRIEF_SEAT_LEVEL=sonnet`); gitleaks or the SDK `--version` printing no version; any of the four tickets no longer Backlog, or a comment or link that narrows or moves its scope (a new comment is information: name it); a `records/*` ref in the code repo (`git -C '<2_Project_Files>' --no-